
Step 1: Launch PowerShell
Open PowerShell as Administrator from the Windows Start menu.
Use the administrator terminal to install and configure WSL.

Step 2: Install WSL
Enter the following command in PowerShell:
wsl --install

Step 3: Restart the System
Restart the computer after WSL installation is completed.

Step 4: Configure Ubuntu
Open Ubuntu from the Start menu after restarting.
Wait for the initial setup and enter a Linux username when prompted.
Enter new UNIX username: amulya

Step 5: Set Linux Password
Create a password for the newly created Linux user.
Enter the password again to confirm it.
New password: ****
Retype new password: ****

Step 6: Update Ubuntu

Step 7: Install GCC
sudo apt install gcc

Step 8: Check GCC Installation
gcc --version

Step 9: Create a C Program
Create a new C source file using the Nano editor.
nano prac1.c

Step 10: Compile the Program
gcc prac1.c -o prac1
Run the compiled program using:
./process




What was acheived?

