Set up a Linux virtual machine to provide the environment for OS development.

2.Configure GCC 
Install and configure GCC to compile C programs.

3.Setup Git Repository 
Create a Git repository to manage and track project files and changes.

4.Create Project Structure 
Organize source code, headers, Makefile, and other project files into proper directories.

5.Understand Shell Architecture 
Study how the shell accepts commands, creates processes, and interacts with the Linux kernel.

